<title>BELGIUM: EU clears takeover of Finnish Chemicals.</title>
<headline>EU clears takeover of Finnish Chemicals.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had cleared the takeover of Finnish Chemicals by two British companies, Prudential Nominees Ltd and HSBC Equity Ltd.</p>
<p>Prudential Nominees is controlled by Prudential Corporation Ltd and HSBC by HSBC Holdings plc.</p>
<p>Finnish Chemicals manufactures and supplies pulping and bleaching chemicals for the pulp and paper industries.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement that UPM-Kymmene Corp and Nokia Corp Corp had agreed to sell their shares in Finnish Chemicals in a management buy-out that would result in control passing to the two Briish-based firms.</p>
<p>The two would have veto rights over some Finnish Chemicals decisions, it said.</p>
<p>Both Prudential and HSBC are fund managers and are not active in any of the markets in which Finnish Chemicals is involved, the Commission said. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
